From 09b52349f3364a6378e7cc00498c21f596167df9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 19:52:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v1.4.4: security-review remediation round 2 (deferred
 LOW / defense-in-depth)

Clears the remaining LOW items from the v1.4.2 multi-agent review (HIGH/MEDIUM
were v1.4.3). None was a live vulnerability. Fixes apply to both build variants
except the AI Advisor items, which are RTCONFIG_REAPER_MCP-gated (MCP build only).

Traffic Analyzer (rtrafd - both variants):
- Harden the persistent history db against a hostile USB mount: db_save creates
  the temp with O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_WRONLY|O_NOFOLLOW,0600 (published atomically via
  rename), db_load opens O_RDONLY|O_NOFOLLOW, and both the jffs/usb store dirs are
  lstat-checked (dir_ok) so a planted symlink can't redirect writes and history is
  never world-readable.

Dashboard (www/Main_ReaperDash.asp - both variants):
- Stop eval()-ing the three stock CPU/temp/ports responses; a pickJSON() extractor
  + JSON.parse (plain regex for the temp string) parses them as inert data. The
  emitters were confirmed to be single-line double-quoted JSON, so behaviour is
  unchanged.

AI Advisor (httpd/web.c + www/Reaper_Advisor.asp - MCP build only):
- CSRF: reaper_mcp.cgi is NOT in the (prebuilt/closed) web_hook.o mime_referers
  whitelist, so do_referer stays 0 and referer_check() never runs for it; do_auth
  only proves the login cookie. Since the closed table can't be edited, gate the
  two security-relevant state changes (deprovision, usb_unenroll) on proof of the
  current arming code (rmcp_require_code: constant-time, shared lockout accounting),
  mirroring the provision-rotate guard. The arming page prompts for the code.
- Boot sweep: reaper_mcp_boot_sweep() in start_services removes a stale LAN
  INPUT...ACCEPT rule + /tmp/reaper_mcp/session left by an unclean rmcpd exit
  (SIGKILL/SEGV); reconstructs the exact rule from lan_ifname + rmcp_port + the
  session's strictly-validated client. Never starts the daemon.

Both v1.4.4 images built + verified (noMCP zero-trace clean); deferred build-flags
item remains in the lean repo docs/BACKLOG.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
